## LeetCode 169 - Majority Element

## My first approach:
HashMap → count frequency
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)

## Optimal approach:
Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)

## Boyer-Moore Algorithm
-- If count == 0, make the current value the candidate.
-- If the current value matches the candidate → count++.
-- If the current value doesn't match the candidate → count--.
-- After traversing the array, return the candidate.

Core idea:
Majority element appears more than n/2 times,
so different elements can cancel each other,
but the majority element will survive.

SOLUTION: 
class MajorityElement {

    // Approach 1: HashMap
    // Time: O(n)
    // Space: O(n)
    public static int majorityElementHashMap(int[] nums) {

        int n = nums.length;
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

        for (int num : nums) {
            map.put(num, map.getOrDefault(num, 0) + 1);
        }

        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : map.entrySet()) {
            if (entry.getValue() > n / 2) {
                return entry.getKey();
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }

    // Approach 2: Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm
    // Time: O(n)
    // Space: O(1)
    public static int majorityElement(int[] nums) {

        int candidate = 0;
        int count = 0;

        for (int num : nums) {

            if (count == 0) {
                candidate = num;
            }

            if (num == candidate) {
                count++;
            } else {
                count--;
            }
        }

        return candidate;
    }
}
